The patches in this directory and in upstream/ modify WAMR (the WebAssembly Micro Runtime,
github.com/bytecodealliance/wasm-micro-runtime). WAMR is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 with the LLVM
exception (SPDX: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception), and these patches are under the same licence, not under this
repository's MIT licence:

    wamr-2.4.5-psram-exec.patch
    wamr-local-const-symbol-map.patch
    wamr-local-esp-cache-msync.patch
    wamr-local-no-lwip.patch
    wamr-local-os-self-thread.patch
    upstream/0001-aot-keep-the-target-symbol-maps-const.patch
    upstream/0001-esp-idf-map-PSRAM-AOT-code-on-the-instruction-bus.patch
    upstream/0001-xtensa-fix-L32R-relocation-lost-to-strict-aliasing.patch

The patches in upstream/ were offered to WAMR; their status is WAMR's own issue and pull request tracker. Everything
else in this directory (the benches, scripts, CMake files and notes) is this repository's own work, under MIT.

No WAMR source file is copied here, and nothing here fetches WAMR: the WebAssembly checks take a WAMR source tree
from WAMR_TREE, which is meant to be WAMR at its pinned commit with these patches applied.
